1
00:04:57,142 --> 00:05:03,142
The hottest chick in town just switched bodies with
the luckiest loser in the world.

2
00:09:54,285 --> 00:10:00,285
The Hot Chick is a comedy, fantasy film directed by Tom Brady.

3
00:14:51,428 --> 00:14:57,428
Not only is Jessica Spencer the most popular girl in
school -- she is also the meanest.

4
00:19:48,571 --> 00:19:54,571
But things change for the attractive teen when a freak accident involving a cursed pair of earrings and a
chance encounter at a gas station causes her to switch bodies with Clive, a sleazy crook.

5
00:24:45,714 --> 00:24:51,714
Jessica, in the form of the repulsive Clive, struggles to adjust to this radical
alteration and sets out to get her own body back before the upcoming prom.

6
00:29:42,857 --> 00:29:48,857
Jessica, played by Rob Schneider.

7
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:46,000
April, played by Anna Faris.

8
00:39:37,142 --> 00:39:43,142
Billy, played by Matthew Lawrence.

9
00:44:34,285 --> 00:44:40,285
Jake, played by Eric Christian Olsen.

10
00:49:31,428 --> 00:49:37,428
Stan, played by Robert Davi.

11
00:54:28,571 --> 00:54:34,571
Carol, played by Melora Hardin.

12
00:59:25,714 --> 00:59:31,714
The Hot Chick is a 2002 American fantasy comedy film directed by Tom Brady, written by Brady and Rob Schneider, and
starring Schneider, Anna Faris, Matthew Lawrence, Eric Christian Olsen, Robert Davi and Michael O'Keefe.

13
01:04:22,857 --> 01:04:28,857
The film follows Jessica Spencer, a mean-spirited cheerleader who
switches bodies with incompetent criminal Clive Maxtone.

14
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
When Jessica discovers that the switch was caused by a pair of enchanted earrings she had stolen, she enlists
the help of her friends to get the earrings back together before the switch becomes permanent.

15
01:14:17,142 --> 01:14:23,142
Adam Sandler served as executive producer and made an uncredited cameo appearance as the Mambuza
Bongo Player, a character based on one played by Schneider on Saturday Night Live.

16
01:19:14,285 --> 01:19:20,285
Principal photography began in March 2002 in Los Angeles and concluded in May.

17
01:24:11,428 --> 01:24:17,428
The Hot Chick was theatrically released in the United States on December
13, 2002, and grossed $55 million against a $34M budget.

18
01:29:08,571 --> 01:29:14,571
It received generally negative reviews from critics.

19
01:34:05,714 --> 01:34:11,714
The film explores themes of sexual identity, high
school, friendship, jewelry, identity.

20
01:39:02,857 --> 01:39:08,857
The tone is lighthearted.
